# MOVEMENT IV — file 75: b201-240 = CODA.
# [Q] b201-208 the MOTTO returns in G minor, ff (Gm, Cm) - the major of
#     the recapitulation is snatched away - then the CELL sinks into the
#     cellos and basses, p - pp, ending in augmentation (CELL4).
# [R] b209-216 G MAJOR, pp, string tremolo over a cello G pedal: hn1
#     sings the CELL in major (CELLM4; the f#4 is a hand-stopped note,
#     veiled, intended), cl1 answers in D, fl1 takes it up 8va, fl1+ob1
#     close with CELLcad in major.
# [S] b217-224 the CELLM as 8th ostinato rises through the strings
#     vc (b217) - va (b219) - vn2 (b221) - vn1 (b223, on D), winds and
#     horns pile up, cresc. p - f.
# [T] b225-232 APOTHEOSIS ff: CELLM in quarters in fl/ob/cl (G - C - D -
#     G) against the same CELLM in 8ths in the violins and the 16th
#     ostinato (L4) in the basses; horns/trumpets fanfare on their
#     natural notes, timpani.
# [U] b233-240 CELLcad in major, augmented then in 8ths, in five
#     octaves; G - D7 strokes; b239 held G-major chord, b240 unison G.

